  SAT:[{id:'s1',type:'mcq',prompt:'Which choice most logically completes the text?',passage:'Researchers studying urban trees found that trees planted along heavily traveled streets often experience different growing conditions from trees in nearby parks. The scientists measured soil temperature, moisture, and canopy growth over several seasons.',choices:['Street trees always grow faster than park trees.','Local conditions can influence how urban trees develop.','Park trees require no maintenance after planting.','Traffic is the only factor affecting tree growth.'],correct:1},{id:'s2',type:'mcq',prompt:'Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?',passage:'A small archive digitized its collection of historical letters so that researchers could consult fragile documents without repeatedly handling the originals. The project also made the collection accessible to students living far from the archive.',choices:['To argue that physical archives should close','To explain two benefits of digitizing a collection','To criticize students for using digital sources','To compare two unrelated archives'],correct:1}],
